#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0687 expect=violation domain=ADDL
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#note "Positive control, and the regression pin for the value_is_reference misuse. The row is the same one CDISC-AD0687-invalid-ADDL uses: DEVIPDT (22281) is greater than DEVXPDT (21915), so the rule must report exactly once. Before the fix the leaf carried value_is_reference:true, which lowered to DEVIPDT > colref(DEVXPDT); colref reads the column NAMED BY DEVXPDT's cell content, ColumnVector.resolvedObject hands the first hop the cell's string form 21915, no column is named 21915, so colref resolved to null and Primitives.comparison returned false on every row - the rule could NEVER fire. This fixture yielded 0 violations before the fix and 1 after. The CDISC twin CDISC-AD0687 has the identical Check WITHOUT the flag and was tested, which is exactly why the PMDA defect survived two reviews."
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=01-701-1015
dataset ADDL
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col SPDEVID type=Char
col DEVIPDT type=Num
col DEVXPDT type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | DEV01 | 22281 | 21915
---
